DEPT® is a Growth Invention company built to help the world’s most ambitious brands grow faster. Operating at the intersection of technology and marketing, our 4,000+ specialists deliver growth invention services across Brand & Media, Experience, Commerce, CRM, and Technology & Data. We’re 50|50 tech and marketing, partner-led, and first to move. Clients include Google, Lufthansa, Meta, eBay, and OpenAI. We have been certified B Corp and Climate Neutral since 2021.

JOB PURPOSE

This role is part of our Experience & Engineering team based in the Netherlands. We combine our skills in developing future-ready technical solutions with our expertise in creating beautiful designs to deliver exceptional and engaging digital experiences that build lasting relationships with our clients like Gant, Inter Milan, bol.com and Just Eat Takeaway.
We are looking for a DevOps Engineer who can build the best cloud platforms for our clients and project teams and can maintain our existing solutions in the smartest way possible. Someone who can switch gears quickly and knows how to come up with automatic workflows to help our teams to accelerate in their work.

As a DevOps Engineer, you search together with your colleagues for the best solutions which you independently translate to the perfect end result. You are responsible for building next level cloud platforms and setting up CI/CD pipelines. You work closely with your SRE colleagues to handover the operations to them. You know how to create long-term simplicity and automate everything so your team can deliver quality to our clients. Technology is transforming fast and that is why we are looking for someone who is eager and motivated to work and experiment with new techniques.

WHAT YOU'LL DO

• Own the infrastructure implementation/migration process from sprint 0 to go-live;

• Collaborate to support a smooth integration and long-term operational efficiency;

• Ensure best practices are established and deliver high quality work;

• Collaborate effectively with our clients teams, including developers questions, to facilitate cross-team communication and ensure a seamless transition;

• Troubleshoot and solve technical issues that may arise during the implementation/migration;

WHAT YOU BRING

• Previous experience as a DevOps Engineer (or similar role);

• Multi-cloud platform experience (Microsoft Azure, AWS and/or GCP);

• Experience with DevOps tooling for CI/CD, orchestration and monitoring like Azure DevOps, GitHub, Datadog, Cloudflare etc.;

• Understanding of Cloud Security & Networking;

• Experience with Infra-As-Code (i.e. Terraform);

• The ability & ambition to take ownership of your projects;

• Working proficiency in English;

WE OFFER

• Great benefits that vary based on the country from which you choose to apply. Feel free to ask about the specific benefits available in your location.

• A flexible, hybrid working policy.

• A rewarding, supportive and healthy company culture.

• A reputation for doing good. DEPT® has been a Certified B Corp® since 2021 and named ‘Agency of the Year’ at both The Lovies and The Webby Awards.

• Awesome clients. Whether big or small, local or global — at DEPT® you’ll get the opportunity to work with clients of all sizes and across all industries. And we celebrate all of our successes together!

• Global annual DEPT® Cares Month in which employees come together and donate their skills to support local charities.

• The opportunity for possibility. We want to enable you to do what you do best and help you develop your skills further with training, development and certifications.

WHY DEPT®?

We are a Growth Invention company built to help the world’s most ambitious brands grow faster. Operating at the intersection of technology and marketing, we create what is next by pioneering ideas, acting fast, and moving further because standing still just is not in our DNA.

We are drawn to people who stay curious, move with intent, and never stop inventing. Our culture runs on three values: better together, relentlessly curious, and get sh*t done. It is how we work, how we grow, and how we make things that matter.

At DEPT®, you will find the freedom to explore, the space to collaborate, and the trust to make a real impact for our clients, for each other, and for the world we are helping to build.

DIVERSITY, EQUITY & INCLUSION

At DEPT®, we take pride in creating an inclusive workplace where everyone has an equal opportunity to thrive. We actively seek to recruit, develop, nurture, and retain talented individuals from diverse backgrounds, with varying skills and perspectives.

Not sure you meet all qualifications? Apply, and let us decide! Research shows that women and members of underrepresented groups tend not to apply for jobs when they think they may not meet every requirement, when in fact they do. We believe in giving everyone a fair chance to shine.

We also encourage you to reach out to us and discuss any reasonable adjustments we can make to support you throughout the recruitment process and your time with us.

Want to know more about our dedication to diversity, equity, and inclusion? Check out our efforts here .

We’re looking for a confident and empathic Full-Cycle Sales Representative to join the team of one of our clients. In this role, you’ll own the whole sales cycle: from the first call with an inbound lead to closing the deal and collecting payment on the spot. The ideal candidate feels at home on the phone, explains product value in plain words to non-technical business owners, and turns hesitation into a clear “yes.”
Ready to close your next deal? Let’s see what it takes 💛

What you will do:

• Contact inbound leads within 5 minutes of their request via phone or email, qualify decision-makers, and pitch the product’s value;

• Run up to 5 focused product demos per day, handle objections in real time, and collect payment directly on the call;

• Make around 20 targeted outbound calls daily from curated lead lists, using multi-touch outreach across phone and email to connect with business owners and general managers;

• Keep records of calls, demos, pipeline stages, and notes in the CRM for accurate forecasting and zero lead leakage;

• Use internal spreadsheets, formulas, filters, and digital workspaces (Slack, Notion, CRM, AI tools like Claude and ChatGPT) to structure your day, prioritize accounts, and make your outreach more efficient.

What you need to succeed in this role:

• C1 English with exceptional spoken and written communication: clear, neutral delivery, confidence over the phone, and comfort leading structured video meetings;

• Ability to follow brand tone-of-voice guidelines, balancing empathy, trust, active listening, and clear explanations of product concepts for non-technical business owners;

• High emotional intelligence and confidence in handling resistance, hesitant buyers, and challenging conversations calmly and constructively;

• Self-direction: you follow up on active leads proactively, hit daily activity targets, and take responsibility for your quota;

• Strong attention to detail, solid time management, and strict adherence to outreach timelines and response SLAs;

• Quick adaptation to modern software (Slack, Notion, CRMs, dialers, and AI productivity tools);

• Comfort in a fast-moving, high-intensity startup environment where priorities and scripts change often;

• A natural drive to solve issues on your own and pick up product updates from internal documentation before escalating to management.

Will be a plus:

• Previous experience in full-cycle B2B or SaaS sales;

• Hands-on experience communicating with US-based customers;

• Solid knowledge of Excel or Google Sheets;

• Ability to quickly pull key insights out of any information;

• Drive for self-development, learning, and continuous improvement.

Benefits:

• Fixed schedule: Monday–Friday, 09:00–18:00 or 12:00–21:00 (Pacific/Gambier, UTC−9);

• Fully remote cooperation;

• Cooperation on a fast-growing B2B SaaS product;

